{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777790102,"nonce":"qLYLGuOk0bPGZDab1UlOFKOruPs=","title":"Outreach: software-heritage.org submission","message":"Submit UC2 v3 to Software Heritage (https://www.softwareheritage.org/) for institutional preservation. Free, permanent, and provides a SWHID (Software Heritage Identifier) that can be cited in academic papers and CV-grade work.\n\nWhy this matters for UC2 specifically:\n- Software Heritage actively preserves abandoned/historical software — a revival project of a 1992 archiver fits their mission perfectly\n- Inclusion gives the project a citable, permanent identifier (swh:1:dir:...) that survives any GitHub/Gitea outage or account closure\n- Cross-references the original UC2 Pro source (already in their archive from the 2015 Bezemer release) to the v3 revival, completing the preservation chain\n- Adds 'archived in Software Heritage' badge to README — institutional credibility signal\n\nSteps:\n1. Save UC2 GitHub URL to https://archive.softwareheritage.org/save/\n2. Verify successful crawl (usually within hours)\n3. Add SWHID badge to README\n4. (Optional) Submit a SWH Catalog entry linking v3 to the original 1992-1996 releases","files":null}]}